The new ThriftRequest(String, String, String, Socket, Map) overload conflicts with the existing ThriftRequest(String, String, SocketAddress, SocketAddress, Map) constructor. The previously valid source expression new ThriftRequest("method", "service", null, null, emptyMap()) is now ambiguous. Remove the conflicting newly added five-argument overload and use the unambiguous six-argument constructor or a distinctly named factory for internal calls that supply separate identities. Preserve every pre-existing public constructor signature and behavior. Do not solve the issue by requiring casts or non-null addresses at old call sites.

Update the existing decorator and focused getter/request tests accordingly. Add a compilation-backed regression test that contains the exact old five-argument null-address call with no casts and verifies its expected legacy/logical service-name and null-address behavior. Keep current sync/async agent, default/preview/dual, duration metric identity, and explicit library-wrapper coverage intact. This is only the overload compatibility correction; do not add unrelated cleanup, conformance changes, public configuration, or automatic library service discovery. Run the narrowest relevant spotlessApply directly before targeted validation and report any actual blocker. Leave the review finding unresolved until the fix is verified.

