@copilot Update this PR directly with the following comment-only clarification in instrumentation/thrift-0.13/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/thrift/v0_13/ThriftSingletons.java. Preserve all code and runtime behavior, the existing base and draft state, and the rpcMethodPrefix documentation/parameter refinement already present. Do not create another PR.

In serviceNames.computeValue, replace the existing comment immediately above the loop over current.getTypeParameters() with these two lines:

```java
// Generated processors declare Processor<I extends Iface> or
// AsyncProcessor<I extends AsyncIface>; the bound identifies the service.
```

Immediately before the if (iface.isInterface() ...) condition, after Class<?> iface = (Class<?>) bound;, add:

```java
// Both the processor and its bound interface must belong to the same service.
```

Keep the change limited to these explanatory comments. The first explains the generated generic shape being inspected; the second explains the common enclosing-service check. Do not refactor or rename code, change tests or documentation elsewhere, or add historical change rationale. Run the narrowest applicable spotlessApply and verify the resulting diff is comment-only. No behavioral test changes are needed.

